From: pocket-debs <masterxq@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 10:37:04 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] taskpanel: show back instead of close while the active window can go back
Description:
 WindowUtil follows the back navigation state of every window through
 kde_back_navigation_shell_v1 (activeWindowCanGoBack) and can ask the
 compositor to go back in the active window (goBackInActiveWindow()). The
 state is reported by applications through kde_back_navigation_v1.
 .
 The navigation bar shows a back arrow in place of the close button while
 the active window can go back, and tapping it goes back in that window.
 Hiding the on-screen keyboard keeps priority. Without the protocol in the
 compositor or in the application the button closes the window as before.
Forwarded: no
License: GPL-2.0-or-later (as the patched files; new files GPL-2.0-or-later, protocol XML file MIT)
Last-Update: 2026-11-27
---
